        "original_id": "5497dee0-7344-5e05-a0ac-5af424c312b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Frears, Christopher Hampton, John Malkovich, Glenn Close, Uma Thurman, Meryl Streep, Bryan Greenberg, Pierre Choderlos de Laclos\n- Films: Mary Reilly, Dangerous Liaisons, Prime\n- Publications and Works: British Vogue, Les liaisons dangereuses\n- Topics: film adaptations, cast and crew re-teaming\n\nFacts:\n- In December 1985 and May 1986, Uma Thurman appeared on the covers of British Vogue.\n- In 1988, Dangerous Liaisons was released as an American historical drama film.\n- In 1988, Dangerous Liaisons was based on Christopher Hampton's play Les liaisons dangereuses, which adapted Pierre Choderlos de Laclos's 18th-century French novel Les Liaisons dangereuses.\n- In 1988, Uma Thurman starred in Dangerous Liaisons.\n- The film Mary Reilly reunited director Stephen Frears, screenwriter Christopher Hampton, and actors John Malkovich and Glenn Close from the Oscar-winning Dangerous Liaisons.\n- In 2005, Prime was released as an American romantic comedy-drama film.\n- Prime starred Uma Thurman, Meryl Streep, and Bryan Greenberg.",
